Now I see the key issue. `N_SSML_STACK` is 20. In `GetVoiceAttributes`, when processing an opening tag (not closing), it does `ssml_sp = &ssml_stack[n_ssml_stack++]` without checking if `n_ssml_stack` is already at the maximum (20). This means if we have more than 19 nested SSML tags that add stack frames (like `<voice>` or `<s xml:lang="...">`), we'll write past the end of the `ssml_stack` array - a heap-buffer-overflow WRITE.

